MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
GS-09:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the next lower grade level GS-07 or pay band in the federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate performing duties such as: 1) Analyzing legal correspondence, pleadings, and documents to verify factual and legal content in preparation for court proceedings;
2) Preparing, maintaining, and managing client case files within a case management system for courts-martial or administrative separation boards;
3) Conducting legal research, investigation, interviews, and other forms of information gathering to make recommendations on legal proceedings; and
4) Developing formal presentations, trainings, or reference material regarding legal or administrative procedures for an organization. GS-11:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the next lower grade level GS-09 or pay band in the federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate performing duties such as: 1) Preparing forms, standard legal documents (e.g., Clemency, witness requests, discovery requests, etc.), and routine correspondence;
2) Preparing, maintaining, and managing client case files and documentation for legal proceedings in accordance with statutory or regulatory requirements;
3) Researching legal documents such as pleadings, motions, requests for members vior dire, responses to similar documents;
4) Training subordinates on case file maintenance and management; and
5) Conducting investigations and interviewing clients/witnesses to obtain and verify information to formulate appropriate legal positions. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.
